meta {
  name: Ask a scoped question
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/chat
  body: json
}

body:json {
  {
    "message": "{{askQuestion}}",
    "scope": { "source_ids": [], "doc_ids": [], "tags": ["{{scopeTag}}"] }
  }
}

docs {
  Server-Sent Events, like the unscoped ask. The scope is resolved once, before any search,
  into a filter applied inside both the vector and full-text queries — so this genuinely
  searches less rather than discarding results afterwards. Live tools for connectors outside
  the scope are not offered on this turn, which is where the saved round-trips come from.

  A scoped "no results" is reported as "not in the sources you scoped to", never as "the
  organisation never learned this" — the model is told it only searched a slice.
}
